---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Submission form. Paste the form URL here once it is live. The Submit step
// renders a link when this is set, and a "coming soon" note while it is empty.
const SUBMISSION_FORM_URL = "https://forms.gle/tFnPUknXHUAgmhhA9";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MOOSE Hackathon 2026 — Problem Statement"
  description="MOOSE Hackathon 2026 individual track: build a clockless neuromorphic pacemaker in MOOSE within a 100-neuron budget."
  url="https://mooseneuro.org/news/hackathon2026"
  ogType="article"
>
  <style is:inline>
    @import url("https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@500;600&display=swap");
  </style>

  <div class="hack-page">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner p-12">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">
            <span class="dot"><span class="ping"></span></span>
            Hackathon open now
          </div>
          <h1>MOOSE Hackathon 2026</h1>
          <p class="tagline">
            Fire up your synapses. Build a model, and let your simulation do the
            talking.
          </p>
          <div class="meta-row">
            <div class="meta-pill">
              <span class="label">Hackathon starts</span>
              <span class="value mono">15 Aug, 10:00am IST</span>
            </div>
            <div class="meta-pill">
              <span class="label">Hackathon closes</span>
              <span class="value mono">30 Aug, 11:59pm IST</span>
            </div>
            <div class="meta-pill">
              <span class="label">Submission</span>
              <span class="value mono">Individual · GitHub</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- BREADCRUMB -->
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <div class="breadcrumb-inner">
        <a href="/news">All News</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="current">MOOSE Hackathon 2026 — Problem Statement</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYOUT -->
    <div class="layout">
      <!-- MAIN: PROBLEM -->
      <main class="card problem-card">
        <div class="kicker">Problem statement</div>
        <h2 class="problem-title">Neuromorphic Oscillatorr</h2>

        <div class="section">
          <h2 class="section-h">
            <span class="icon">
              <svg
                width="14"
                height="14"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                ><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"></rect><path
                  d="M9 9h6v6H9z"></path><path
                  d="M9 2v2M15 2v2M9 20v2M15 20v2M2 9h2M2 15h2M20 9h2M20 15h2"
                ></path></svg
              >
            </span>
            The Scenario
          </h2>
          <p>
            A leading semiconductor firm is developing an ultra-low-power,
            implantable neuromorphic chip designed to serve as a neonatal
            cardiac pacemaker. Instead of using power-hungry, traditional
            digital microcontrollers that rely on high-frequency clock crystals,
            this chip utilizes a hardware network of sub-threshold analog
            artificial spiking neurons. To validate the silicon layout and
            stress-test the circuit dynamics before committing to an expensive
            chip fabrication run (tape-out), your team must design, simulate,
            and optimize this analog network architecture within the MOOSE
            engine.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
          <h2 class="section-h">
            <span class="icon">
              <svg
                width="14"
                height="14"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                ><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M8 12h8M12 8v8"
                ></path></svg
              >
            </span>
            The Objective
          </h2>
          <p>
            Your goal is to construct a population-based, neuromorphic
            oscillator in MOOSE that functions as a highly dependable silicon
            macro-pulse generator. The network must be divided into two
            distinct, competing pools of circuits (representing opposing phases
            of a clock cycle or cardiac muscle pulse). When Pool A is highly
            active, it must completely suppress Pool B, and vice versa. This
            mutual, alternating hardware tug-of-war must create a stable,
            rhythmic anti-phase pattern, functioning as an ultra-reliable,
            clockless pacemaker.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
          <h2 class="section-h">
            <span class="icon">
              <svg
                width="14"
                height="14"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                ><path
                  d="M12 2l3 6 6 .9-4.5 4.3 1 6.3L12 16.5 6.5 19.5l1-6.3L3 8.9 9 8z"
                ></path></svg
              >
            </span>
            Rules &amp; Constraints
          </h2>

          <div class="constraint">
            <div class="c-icon">
              <svg
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"><path d="M2 12h4l3-8 4 16 3-8h6"></path></svg
              >
            </div>
            <div class="c-body">
              <strong>Tonic bias only</strong>
              <p>
                The driving input bias current (inject) entering your electronic
                neurons must be completely static and constant. The input bias
                cannot oscillate. You are forbidden from using external
                electronic sine waves, function generators, or digital clock
                pulses to force the rhythm. The oscillation must emerge purely
                from the internal non-linear equations and feedback loops of the
                silicon layout.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="constraint">
            <div class="c-icon">
              <svg
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                ><path d="M12 3v18M6 8h4M6 16h4M14 8h4M14 16h4"></path></svg
              >
            </div>
            <div class="c-body">
              <strong>Dale's Law compliance</strong>
              <p>
                A single neuron circuit cannot express both excitatory and
                inhibitory behaviors. If a hardware sub-population is designated
                as Excitatory (E), it can only form forward excitatory synapse
                lines (<span class="mono">exc_syn</span>). If it is Inhibitory
                (I), it can only form inhibitory synapse lines (<span
                  class="mono">inh_syn</span
                >). You could budget for inhibitory neurons in each Pool from
                within the 100 neuron budget.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="constraint">
            <div class="c-icon">
              <svg
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                ><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="1"></rect><path
                  d="M9 3v2M15 3v2M9 19v2M15 19v2M3 9h2M3 15h2M19 9h2M19 15h2"
                ></path></svg
              >
            </div>
            <div class="c-body">
              <strong>The 100-neuron silicon budget</strong>
              <p>
                To minimize power consumption and silicon real estate on the
                chip, your entire neuromorphic core has a strict ceiling of
                exactly 100 neuron circuits total.
              </p>
              <div class="budget-grid" aria-hidden="true">
                {Array.from({ length: 100 }).map(() => <span />)}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="constraint">
            <div class="c-icon">
              <svg
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                ><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="9" rx="1.5"></rect><path
                  d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4"></path></svg
              >
            </div>
            <div class="c-body">
              <strong>Fixed hardwired connectome</strong>
              <p>
                Once your synaptic routing matrix (the hardwired lines linking
                the circuits) is established at millisecond zero, you cannot
                alter routing paths, rewire gates, or change weights during
                runtime to alter the chip's behavior.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section" style="margin-bottom:0;">
          <h2 class="section-h">
            <span class="icon">
              <svg
                width="14"
                height="14"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                ><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"
                ></circle></svg
              >
            </span>
            Submission Requirements
          </h2>
          <p>
            Participants must submit the link to their GitHub repository. The
            repository must contain:
          </p>
          <ul class="req-list">
            <li>
              <span class="check">✓</span> The script(s) used to implement the model.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="check">✓</span> A descriptive README file explaining the
              model, methodology, and how to run the code.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="check">✓</span> Output graphs of the neuronal subpopulations,
              such as raster plots or voltage traces — saved as PNG images and included
              in the README for reference.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </main>

      <!-- SIDEBAR -->
      <aside class="sidebar">
        <div class="card side-card">
          <h3><span class="em">📅</span> Key Dates</h3>
          <div class="date-row">
            <span class="d-label">Registration closed</span>
            <span class="d-value past">14 Aug, 11:59pm IST</span>
          </div>
          <div class="date-row">
            <span class="d-label">Hackathon starts</span>
            <span class="d-value">15 Aug, 10:00am IST</span>
          </div>
          <div class="date-row">
            <span class="d-label">Hackathon closes</span>
            <span class="d-value">30 Aug, 11:59pm IST</span>
          </div>
          <div class="countdown" id="countdown">
            <div class="cd-unit">
              <div class="cd-num" id="cd-d">–</div>
              <div class="cd-lbl">Days</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cd-unit">
              <div class="cd-num" id="cd-h">–</div>
              <div class="cd-lbl">Hrs</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cd-unit">
              <div class="cd-num" id="cd-m">–</div>
              <div class="cd-lbl">Min</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cd-unit">
              <div class="cd-num" id="cd-s">–</div>
              <div class="cd-lbl">Sec</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card side-card">
          <h3><span class="em">🏆</span> Prizes</h3>
          <p class="prize-body">
            <strong>Top 3 winners</strong> and <strong>2 runner-ups</strong> receive
            a certificate plus MOOSE merchandise. All participants who successfully
            complete the hackathon receive MOOSE merchandise.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card side-card">
          <h3><span class="em">🔗</span> Resources</h3>
          <div class="resource-chips">
            <a href="/">Website</a>
            <a href="/docs/html/">Docs</a>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/MooseNeuro/moose-examples"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Examples</a
            >
            <a
              href="https://github.com/MooseNeuro/moose-notebooks"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Notebooks</a
            >
            <a
              href="https://github.com/MooseNeuro/moose-core"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">moose-core</a
            >
            <a
              href="https://github.com/MooseNeuro/jardesigner"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Jardesigner</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card side-card">
          <h3><span class="em">🚀</span> How to Submit</h3>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>
              <div class="s-title">Write &amp; test</div>
              <div class="s-desc">
                Notebook(s) must run top-to-bottom via <span class="mono"
                  >Run All</span
                >, no manual steps. Add a short markdown cell above each step
                explaining it.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <div class="s-title">Push to GitHub</div>
              <div class="s-desc">
                Public repo named <span class="mono">moose2026hackathon</span> holding
                your notebook(s), data files, and <span class="mono"
                  >README.md</span
                >. Include everything the notebook needs and reference it with
                relative paths.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <div class="s-title">README</div>
              <div class="s-desc">
                Judges use this to gauge your understanding, so be precise:
                problem statement, approach, step-by-step, dependencies, file
                structure, how to run, expected output, closing remark.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <div class="s-title">Submit</div>
              <div class="s-desc">
                Paste your repository URL into the{" "}
                {
                  SUBMISSION_FORM_URL ? (
                    <a
                      class="s-form-link"
                      href={SUBMISSION_FORM_URL}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener"
                    >
                      Submission form
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    "submission form"
                  )
                }
                {
                  !SUBMISSION_FORM_URL && (
                    <span class="s-form-soon">Form link coming soon.</span>
                  )
                }
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="card side-card">
          <h3><span class="em">📋</span> Rules</h3>
          <ul class="rules-list">
            <li><span class="bullet">·</span> Individual submissions only.</li>
            <li><span class="bullet">·</span> Repo must be public.</li>
            <li>
              <span class="bullet">·</span> Late fixes after the deadline don't count
              toward the top 5.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hack-page {
    --bg-hero: #111827;
    --bg-hero-glow: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.28);
    --accent: #6366f1;
    --accent-dark: #4338ca;
    --accent-soft: #eef0fe;
    --violet: #8b5cf6;
    --card-bg: #ffffff;
    --card-border: #e5e7eb;
    --bg-subtle: #f9fafb;
    --text-primary: #111827;
    --text-secondary: #4b5563;
    --text-muted: #9ca3af;
    --good: #16a34a;

    font-family:
      "Inter",
      -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      sans-serif;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    background: #ffffff;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .hack-page *,
  .hack-page *::before,
  .hack-page *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .mono {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, monospace;
  }
  .hack-page a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* ---------- HERO ---------- */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--bg-hero);
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 76px 32px 56px;
  }
  .hero::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: -140px;
    left: -80px;
    width: 620px;
    height: 620px;
    background: radial-gradient(
      circle,
      var(--bg-hero-glow) 0%,
      rgba(99, 102, 241, 0) 70%
    );
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hero-inner {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    color: #c7d2fe;
    background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.14);
    border: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.35);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 6px 12px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .eyebrow .dot {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-flex;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #16a34a;
  }
  /* Expanding ring, matching the live indicator on the promo banners */
  .eyebrow .dot .ping {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #22c55e;
    opacity: 0.75;
    animation: dotPing 3s cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.2, 1) infinite;
  }
  @keyframes dotPing {
    75%,
    100% {
      transform: scale(2.4);
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }
  .hero h1 {
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 56px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .hero p.tagline {
    color: #c2cbde;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    max-width: 560px;
  }
  .meta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .meta-pill {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    background: rgba(15, 20, 33, 0.72);
    backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
  }
  .meta-pill .label {
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: #a3aec7;
  }
  .meta-pill .value {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #f1f3fb;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .meta-pill .value.mono {
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 40px;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- BREADCRUMB ---------- */
  .breadcrumb {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--card-border);
    padding: 14px 32px;
  }
  .breadcrumb-inner {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .breadcrumb-inner .current {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .breadcrumb-inner a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
  }

  /* ---------- LAYOUT ---------- */
  .layout {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 32px 80px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px;
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: 28px 20px 64px;
    }
  }

  .card {
    background: var(--card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow:
      0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06),
      0 2px 4px -2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
  }

  /* ---------- PROBLEM (MAIN) ---------- */
  .problem-card {
    padding: 36px 40px 44px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .problem-card {
      padding: 26px 20px 32px;
    }
  }

  .kicker {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .problem-title {
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .spec-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--card-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--card-border);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .spec {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 140px;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  }
  .spec:last-child {
    border-right: none;
  }
  .spec .spec-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .spec .spec-value {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .spec {
      flex: 1 1 50%;
      border-right: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--card-border);
    }
  }

  h2.section-h {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    padding-top: 6px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  h2.section-h .icon {
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .section {
    margin-bottom: 34px;
  }
  .section p {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #27324a;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .constraint {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 16px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #eef0f4;
  }
  .constraint:first-of-type {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .constraint .c-icon {
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    border-radius: 9px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    background: #f4f2ff;
    color: var(--violet);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .constraint .c-body strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .constraint .c-body p {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .budget-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(20, 1fr);
    gap: 3px;
    max-width: 260px;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .budget-grid span {
    width: 100%;
    padding-bottom: 100%;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: #e3e0ff;
    display: block;
  }

  .req-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .req-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #27324a;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #eef0f4;
  }
  .req-list li:first-child {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .req-list .check {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 1px;
    background: #ecfdf3;
    color: var(--good);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* ---------- SIDEBAR ---------- */
  .sidebar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    position: sticky;
    top: 84px;
  }
  .side-card {
    padding: 22px 22px 24px;
  }
  .side-card h3 {
